; Plugin loads, dispatches `(echo-tag :hello)` into `wasm:tag`, plugin
; frames the same keyword back, host decodes it against the declared
; `:result keyword`. The `(values …)` block locks the keyword identity
; — without it a regression that returns `:goodbye` (or worse, a string
; instead of a keyword) would pass on a clean diagnostic stream.
(diagnostics)
(values
  (value :index 0 :result :hello))
